WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.818
Begin with the mission objective and decision.

00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:12.129
Define the target, suspected condition, required detail, acceptable uncertainty, authorized area, and who will interpret the result.

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:18.642
Avoid collecting a broad thermal survey when only one bounded question is legitimate.

00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:23.359
Select timing based on target behavior and environmental contrast.

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:30.771
Building, roof, solar, mechanical, electrical, and search-support tasks may need different operating states and times.

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:35.936
Coordinate with qualified personnel who understand the system being observed.

00:00:35.936 --> 00:00:43.348
Altitude, distance, angle, lens, and sensor resolution determine how many detector pixels cover the target.

00:00:43.348 --> 00:00:48.963
Keep within safe and lawful operating limits while collecting sufficient detail.

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:53.231
An attractive overview may be inadequate for measurement.

00:00:53.231 --> 00:01:00.643
Plan coverage, flight speed, stable pauses, orientation, and overlap when mapping or comparison is required.

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:04.461
Use repeatable routes and settings where practical.

00:01:04.461 --> 00:01:10.525
Excessive speed or motion can blur patterns and reduce usable target detail.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:15.691
Complete aircraft, site, weather, battery, payload, storage, and calibration-context checks.

00:01:15.691 --> 00:01:24.451
Define abort criteria for wind, moisture, visibility, equipment warnings, poor contrast, privacy concerns, or an unavailable recovery area.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:27.820
Document the plan and protect privacy.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:36.579
Limit imagery to mission need, avoid unrelated people or private areas, and define access and retention before collection.

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:42.644
Thermal capability does not reduce the need for lawful authority or proportionality.
